 of stress handling, decision under pressure, but anticipating dangerous situations suggests good judgment.\n\nB:\n- Strengths: very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (performance under pressure), good at assessing weather (technical), excellent computer skills (technical). \n- Weaknesses: makes nasty remarks about colleagues (teamwork/communication), relatively weak memory for numbers (technical), regarded as pretentious, sometimes adopts wrong tone (communication). No explicit decision speed.\n\nC:\n- Strengths: can make correct decisions quickly (decision-making), creates positive atmosphere with crew (teamwork), 100% reliability, excellent attention skills, puts concern for others above everything (teamwork/crew care). \n- Weaknesses: difficulty communicating ideas (communication), egocentric (teamwork), not willing to further education (professional development). \n\nD:\n- Strengths: responds to unexpected events adequately (judgment under pressure), can concentrate very well (cognitive), solves problems extremely well (technical/cognitive), takes responsibility seriously (reliability). \n- Weaknesses: considered moody, regarded as loner, arrogance, relatively weak leadership skills, no info on teamwork/communication. \n\nNow evaluate for long-distance pilot: need reliability, decision-making, calm under pressure, teamwork/communication, professional development.\n\nCandidate C seems strong in decision speed, reliability, crew morale, concern for others, but has communication difficulty and egocentric, not willing to further education (long-term suitability). The communication difficulty could be mitigated? But we must weigh.\n\nCandidate B strong in stress handling, conscientious, weather assessment, but poor interpersonal (nasty remarks, wrong tone). That is a serious issue for crew cooperation.\n\nCandidate A strong leadership, anticipates danger, but unfriendly and health concerns. Leadership may offset unfriendly? But unfriendly likely harms